PASS: the disabled trigger retires the sprite with the "no longer targets a sprite" reason and destroys it.

## Re-enable   (trigger-v7-enabled.yml)

$ docs/qa/ac-50k/install.sh trigger-v7-enabled.yml
save 13:45:59.3   HTTP 201 version 11   latency 0.279 s

Hub log, starting 1 s later:
  16:45:59.251  sprite activation: destroy leftover
  16:45:59.733  sprite activation: create
  16:46:00.939  sprite activation: npm prefix
  16:46:02.707  sprite activation: install paseo
  16:46:18.922  sprite activation: bootstrap
  …
  machine 690e8576 spawning within 20 s of the save; alive at 13:46:35 with daemon 35dabe2d (connected 13:46:34.410)
  GET /v1/sprites/trigger-9803bdab-…  -> HTTP 200

OBSERVED, not as the brief predicted: re-enabling activates IMMEDIATELY. It does not wait for the next run.
The save returns in 0.279 s and the activation runs as the usual fire-and-forget job (createSpriteActivation
takes the create branch, since findLiveSpriteMachine returns nothing for the terminated row). This matches
PRD section 6's first row, "Trigger activated with sprite target -> create … ", so it is correct behaviour;
recorded because the scenario expected recreation only on the next arrival. See finding 5.

## Observation: disable while an execution is running

$ docs/qa/ac-50k/run.sh qa-s5-run-2
fire 13:46:42.061
13:46:46.541 exec 44df28b4 status=running   (action=reset; the sprite was recreated at 13:46:34)

$ docs/qa/ac-50k/install.sh trigger-v6-disabled.yml     <- while it is running
save 13:46:46.3   HTTP 201 version 12   latency 1.676 s     <- ACCEPTED, no guard

  [16:46:48.323 +0300] INFO: sprite retired   (machineId 690e8576, reason "trigger no longer targets a sprite")
  machine 690e8576 terminated "trigger no longer targets a sprite" terminated_at 13:46:48.320
  daemon  35dabe2d revoked  offline  disconnected 13:46:48.316
  GET /v1/sprites/trigger-9803bdab-…  -> HTTP 404, about 2 s after the save

The running execution then:
  13:46:54.889 exec 44df28b4 still `running` on daemon 35dabe2d, 6 s after its sprite was destroyed
  13:48:45.069 exec 44df28b4 failed {"reason":"step_idle_timeout"}   run failed step_idle_timeout

  save -> execution terminal: 1 m 58.8 s, which is the trigger's `idle_timeout: 2m` to the second.
  The execution did not fail fast and did not fail as `daemon_timeout` or `sprite_unavailable`; it burned
  its whole idle timeout and then reported the generic idle reason.

  hub_action_completed_at for 44df28b4 is NULL: the auto_archive could not be delivered, the sprite is gone.
  Hub log at terminal:
    [16:48:45.572 +0300] WARN: sprites.release failed
        failureKind: "notFound"   operation: "sprites.release"   component: "daemons"
        diagnostic: { "executionId": "44df28b4-f14f-5e0c-8299-617a62f75e50" }
        err: SpritesError … at Object.release … DaemonDispatchLifecycle.releaseSpriteHold
            … sendPendingHubAction … failAgentExecution … expireExecutionAtCurrentDeadline
  No `daemon.execution.hub-action failed` line (0 in the window).

Reported as findings 1 and 2, not as pass or fail, exactly as the brief asks.
